WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.767
This comparison helps choose the right object.

00:00:02.767 --> 00:00:05.772
A CTE is local to one statement.

00:00:05.772 --> 00:00:08.357
A standard view is shared and live.

00:00:08.357 --> 00:00:11.562
A materialized view is shared and stored.

00:00:11.562 --> 00:00:16.047
Temporary business thresholds usually belong close to the report.

00:00:16.047 --> 00:00:20.577
Stable shared relational meaning often belongs in a standard view.

00:00:20.577 --> 00:00:27.542
Expensive reused summaries may justify materialization if the freshness tradeoff is acceptable.

00:00:27.542 --> 00:00:33.187
A standard view stores a query definition, not a separate copy of the rows.

00:00:33.187 --> 00:00:39.647
Treat the selected columns, names, types, and grain as a contract with downstream users.

00:00:39.647 --> 00:00:46.477
Changing that contract can break dashboards or applications even if the underlying query still runs.
